<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">National and Kapodistrian University of Athens</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1837">1837</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as University of Athens</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The National and Kapodistrian University of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/athens">Athens</a> is the oldest university in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a> and the eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mediterranean">Mediterranean</a>, founded in 1837 under King Otto. Its neoclassical main building in central Athens was designed by Christian Hansen. It became the main centre for training the officials, lawyers, doctors and teachers of the Greek state, and its students were often active in national politics.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/national-and-kapodistrian-university-of-athens.jpg" alt="National and Kapodistrian University of Athens" width="320" height="171" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Thomas Wolf, www.foto-tw.de · CC BY-SA 3.0 de · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Universit%C3%A4t_von_Athen.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
